\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces Control-flow of the dense RI-J and RI-K integral routines, annotated with the underlying equations. The boxes in the top row form the one-time startup phase; everything inside the outer dashed region is re-evaluated in every SCF cycle. Boxes are colored by operation type: blue for host orchestration and interaction with the external SCF library, yellow for pre-computed data held in device memory, orange for dense matrix--matrix products (GEMM), and green for matrix--vector products (GEMV) and element-wise scaling. The inner dashed box marks the loop over occupied orbitals in the RI-K scheme. The Fock/Kohn--Sham assembly is drawn schematically.\relax }}{15}{figure.caption.4}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:dense_ri_flow}{{2}{15}{Control-flow of the dense RI-J and RI-K integral routines, annotated with the underlying equations. The boxes in the top row form the one-time startup phase; everything inside the outer dashed region is re-evaluated in every SCF cycle. Boxes are colored by operation type: blue for host orchestration and interaction with the external SCF library, yellow for pre-computed data held in device memory, orange for dense matrix--matrix products (GEMM), and green for matrix--vector products (GEMV) and element-wise scaling. The inner dashed box marks the loop over occupied orbitals in the RI-K scheme. The Fock/Kohn--Sham assembly is drawn schematically.\relax }{figure.caption.4}{}}
