\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {10}{\ignorespaces Distribution of the signed error in the W4-11 total atomization energies, one violin per Slater-type basis set, with the number of converged reactions given below each label. Method is unrestricted B3LYP (Libxc \texttt  {hyb\_gga\_xc\_b3lyp3}, the VWN3 parametrization) with the dense algorithm. The grid is TA-M4 radial with $n_\mathrm  {rad}=100$ and Lebedev order $L=35$ with robust pruning and uniform radial sizing. The linear dependence threshold of $10^{-4}$ is applied uniformly to all four basis sets. Reference values are the zero-point exclusive, non-relativistic, clamped-nuclei atomization energies of Ref.~\cite  {Karton11w411}. Individual reactions are overlaid as jittered points and the horizontal bar marks the median. The shaded band is the conventional $\pm 1$~kcal/mol window of chemical accuracy. The quantity plotted is the combined basis set and functional error. The quadrature error of Section~\ref {subsec:convergence} is smaller by three to four orders of magnitude and is invisible on this scale. The summary statistics are given in Table~\ref {tab:w411_summary}.\relax }}{24}{figure.caption.14}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:w411_violin}{{10}{24}{Distribution of the signed error in the W4-11 total atomization energies, one violin per Slater-type basis set, with the number of converged reactions given below each label. Method is unrestricted B3LYP (Libxc \texttt {hyb\_gga\_xc\_b3lyp3}, the VWN3 parametrization) with the dense algorithm. The grid is TA-M4 radial with $n_\mathrm {rad}=100$ and Lebedev order $L=35$ with robust pruning and uniform radial sizing. The linear dependence threshold of $10^{-4}$ is applied uniformly to all four basis sets. Reference values are the zero-point exclusive, non-relativistic, clamped-nuclei atomization energies of Ref.~\cite {Karton11w411}. Individual reactions are overlaid as jittered points and the horizontal bar marks the median. The shaded band is the conventional $\pm 1$~kcal/mol window of chemical accuracy. The quantity plotted is the combined basis set and functional error. The quadrature error of Section~\ref {subsec:convergence} is smaller by three to four orders of magnitude and is invisible on this scale. The summary statistics are given in Table~\ref {tab:w411_summary}.\relax }{figure.caption.14}{}}
